  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "Every year, a psychic spy named Joe McMoneagle is said to have gone into a SCIF, a sealed room for classified work, and done \"remote viewing,\" the claimed ability to see distant places with the mind, so that officials would renew the budget of Stargate, the US government's psychic spying programme. The researcher Chris Ramsay tells Michels this without naming a source. In his telling, the demonstrations worked well enough to keep the money coming."
